# Probe reports written while working on the neovim plugin. Every file here deploys
# to the home directory unless it is named, and a report is not configuration.
#
# Written without the leading slash of .gitignore's `/p0*.txt`, because chezmoi
# rejects the whole source state on a leading slash here: `diff`, `status`,
# `managed` and every other command that reads the source state then fail with
# `invalid path`. chezmoi matches a pattern with no slash in the top folder
# only, so both files ignore a report there alone.
p0*.txt
# nvim writes its log to ~/.local/state/nvim/nvim.log, and falls back to
# nvim.log in the working directory when it cannot write there, which can be
# any folder of this repository. A log is not configuration, and this name does
# not begin with a dot, so chezmoi would deploy it from whichever folder it is
# in; `**/` matches it at every depth, the top included.
**/nvim.log
**/__pycache__
